# Automated CI/CD Web Deployment Pipeline

An end-to-end DevOps project demonstrating automated container building, integration testing, and zero-downtime static web deployment using **Docker** and **GitHub Actions**.

## Architecture & Command Flow

Every push to `main` or `master` triggers a two-stage automated pipeline:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Developer Push<br/>(git add / commit / push)"] --> B["GitHub Repo<br/>(.github/workflows)"]
    B --> C{GitHub Actions CI/CD}
    subgraph Stage 1: Build & Test
        C --> D["Build Image<br/>(docker buildx build)"]
        D --> E["Run Container<br/>(docker run -d -p 8080:80)"]
        E --> F["Smoke Test<br/>(curl & grep)"]
    end
    subgraph Stage 2: Deploy
        F -->|Tests Pass| G["Package Artifact<br/>(cp index.html _site/)"]
        G --> H["Deploy Pages<br/>(actions/deploy-pages)"]
    end
    H --> I((Live Website))
```

## Tech Stack
* **Source Control & Cloud IDE:** Git, GitHub, GitHub Codespaces
* **CI/CD Automation:** GitHub Actions (Multi-stage YAML workflow with Buildx caching & concurrency control)
* **Containerization:** Docker (`nginx:alpine` lightweight base image)
* **Hosting / Deployment Target:** GitHub Pages

