## Pipeline Breakdown (What Runs Automatically)

1. **Build & Test Stage (`build-and-test`):**
   * Checks out code (`actions/checkout@v4`) and sets up **Docker Buildx** (`docker/setup-buildx-action@v3`) with GitHub Actions layer caching (`type=gha`).
   * Builds the container image (`docker/build-push-action@v6`) with provenance and SBOM metadata.
   * Launches an isolated container on port `8080`, runs a retry-enabled `curl` check + `grep` content validation, and tears down the container automatically via a `trap cleanup EXIT` hook.
2. **Deploy Stage (`deploy-pages`):**
   * Runs only after `build-and-test` passes on a push to `main` or `master`.
   * Copies `index.html` into `_site/`, uploads the artifact (`actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3`), and deploys it live (`actions/deploy-pages@v4`).

